LNCP — Licensing

This repository intentionally uses different licenses for different parts,
chosen so that anyone may implement the protocol freely, in any language, for
any purpose:

  spec/       CC0 1.0 Universal        see spec/LICENSE
  vectors/    CC0 1.0 Universal        see vectors/LICENSE
  reference/  Apache License 2.0       see reference/LICENSE

In short:

- The SPECIFICATION and the CONFORMANCE VECTORS are dedicated to the public
  domain (CC0). Implementing LNCP never requires permission and never imposes
  a license on your program.

- The REFERENCE LIBRARY (@lncp/core) is permissively licensed under
  Apache-2.0. You may use it directly in commercial or open-source software.

A program that uses or implements LNCP is free to choose its own license.
